I am standing at the checkout.
I take my things and put them on the belt.
The cashier scans them.
It goes very fast!
In Denmark they are very fast in the supermarket.
I hurry to pack the bags.
I put the bread and the milk in one bag.
It is a bit hectic, but I manage it.
"That will be a hundred and fifty kroner," says the cashier.
"Do you want the receipt?" he asks.
"No thank you," I answer.
I pay with my card.
The machine beeps.
I take the bags.
The bags are full.
But now I have food!
